        "body": "Gain 5, Work 2, Harm 3\nRaise: Not done\nCase: normal use - a roughly ten-second DNS outage causes fast failures while a queued child reads a pull request.\nThe shared GitHub read retries with waits totaling seven seconds, then replaces the DNS diagnostic with `GitHub did not answer. Rerun the command.` (`src/forge/repo.py:367` and `src/forge/repo.py:397`). `close._gh` turns that result into a refusal (`src/forge/close.py:908`), so this matcher never sees `error connecting to`. The queue marks the child stopped and does not restart it when the connection returns. The discarded diagnostic is evidence beyond the coordinator's instruction to match the GitHub CLI message.",
